      ":question/id": "12003e8d-c48c-5642-87cc-c7c437d424fc",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-123203",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $r(t)=\u27e86\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5t),\\,{\\sin }^{2}\u2061(5t)\u27e9,$ calculate $r\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We substitute $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right) & =\u27e86\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,{\\sin }^{2}\u2061(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}),\\,{\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)}^{2}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83,\\,\\frac{3}{4}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
